\ Expansion is eager, so `two` arrives flat and `one`'s attribution is already recorded against
\ `two`'s body rather than reachable from `three`'s source. A transitive chain names every level
\ only if the copy carries those records forward.
\
\ Each row's line is the call site the copy replaced, in the body that held it: `one` at line 11
\ inside `two`, `two` at line 12 inside `three`.
\
\ No flags: one golden binds the interpreted and eager suites.

one:   ( s v -- n ) const inline [ stream-write 0 + ] ;
two:   ( s v -- n ) const inline [ one 0 + ] ;
three: ( s v -- n ) [ two 0 + ] ;

stdout 42 three .
